  "id": "ua-pulaski-technical-college-aas-aviation-maintenance",
  "major": "Aviation Maintenance",
  "notes": "Program provides instruction in the general power plant and airframe curricula. Students may seek FAA certification as an aircraft maintenance technician with an airframe rating and/or a power plant rating by completing the certificate curricula, or complete the AAS for additional education to advance into supervisory and inspection positions. The Aviation Maintenance Technology program is accredited by the FAA as an approved Part 147 Maintenance School. CREDIT-RANGE HANDLING: the degree requires 89-92 credit hours; the 'As Needed' TECH 2103V Work Based Instruction (Capstone) is 0-3 hours and is only completed with the program director to make up failed course components, so the lower bound (0) is used, giving a mapped total of 89. Minimum 2.00 cumulative GPA required for graduation. Additional prerequisite courses may be required if minimum placement test scores are not met.",
